## Controller Naming

Always use yarn instead of npm to install packages or run scripts

Prefer joined class names for controllers using the `::` namespace separator. For example, use `class API::UsersController` instead of `class Api::UsersController` or nested module syntax.

Note: `API` is configured as an acronym inflection in `config/initializers/inflections.rb`, which allows Rails to properly handle the namespace.
